<content><![CDATA[<h2 data-style-guide="headline" data-design-treatment="vert" data-primary="8" data-padding="xs" data-border-radius="xs">Lesson 1 Overview</h2><p>HAX sites look like ordinary websites until you sign in. Then a bar at the top gives you tools to edit pages, add pages, and change the whole site. This lesson walks through those tools.</p><h3 data-style-guide="sectionDivider" data-design-treatment="horz-md" data-primary="2" data-padding="xs" data-instructional-action="read">In this lesson</h3><ul data-style-guide="readingRequired" data-design-treatment="reading-required"><li><a href="lesson-1-introduction">Reading a HAX Site</a></li><li><a href="lesson-1-content">Editing a Page</a></li><li><a href="lesson-1-conclusion">Check Your Understanding</a></li></ul>]]></content>
